SET content = content || E'\n\n## Native Ground Forces and Garrison Draft\n\nEvery inhabited planet maintains a native ground-force baseline drawn from its own population. Each turn, this baseline auto-replenishes toward a soft ceiling equal to ``floor(current_population / ground_defense_pop_divisor)`` — closing half of any deficit per turn at the standard ground-force replacement cost. This automatic conscription is free of any player action but never exceeds the population baseline, no matter how many Ground Defense facilities the planet has built.\n\nTo raise a planet''s Ground Defenses above the population baseline — up to the full ``max_ground_defenses`` (population baseline plus every Ground Defense facility bonus) — the owning player must actively **Draft Garrison** on that planet. Each drafted unit costs one ``ground_force_replacement_cost`` from the treasury and is queued as a between-turn order, resolved during the next Economy phase. Building additional Ground Defense facilities therefore only translates into stronger garrisons if the player also pays to fill the extra slots.'
